  "live_records": {
    "q-34832": {
      "dom_id": "step-q34832",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "$\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}\\{[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\})=$",
      "worked_solution": "We start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}5 & -10 & 15 \\\\ -1 & 5 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & -10 & 15 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to basis vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the reduced matrix has $2$ pivot columns (or alternatively, it has exactly $2$ non-zero rows). \n\nTherefore, \n$\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}\\{[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\})=2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
