    "q-35298": {
      "dom_id": "step-q35298",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]\\})=$",
      "worked_solution": "We start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 6 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to basis vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the reduced matrix has $1$ pivot column (or alternatively, it has exactly $1$ non-zero row). \n\nTherefore, \n$\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}\\{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]\\})=1.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
