    "q-79320": {
      "dom_id": "step-q79320",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Determine the dimension of $\\text{Span}\\{[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\\}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, our matrix is already in a row echelon form.\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to basis vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns (or alternatively, $3$ non-zero rows). \n\nTherefore, the dimension of the span is $3.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
